# Direct dependencies of the backend image (see Dockerfile) and of the
# local development environment. Hash-Lock folgt spaeter -- requirements.txt
# is currently a plain `pip freeze` of the resolved tree, not a
# `pip-compile --generate-hashes` lock (see requirements.txt's own header),
# same discipline as Weave-Retrieval's and Weave-Runtime's own requirements.in.
#
# fastapi/uvicorn/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pytest/httpx pins are kept
# identical to Weave-Retrieval's backend/requirements.in -- Weave-Tools is
# the same generation of service (no own database, calls other Weave
# services over HTTP), so there is no reason for its web-framework/test
# stack to drift from theirs.
#
# `mcp` is the official Model Context Protocol Python SDK (PyPI package
# "mcp") -- see app/mcp_server.py's module docstring for how its
# MCPServer/streamable-HTTP surface is used here. 2.x renamed the old
# FastMCP class to MCPServer and reshuffled several submodules (see that
# release's own migration guide, printed by importing the removed
# `mcp.server.fastmcp` module); this pins the exact 2.x release the code was
# actually written and tested against (including a real client-session
# round trip over the streamable-HTTP transport, in-process), not the older
# 1.x FastMCP API most existing tutorials still show.
fastapi==0.141.1
uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4
pydantic==2.13.5
pydantic-settings==2.15.0
httpx==0.28.1
pytest==9.1.1
mcp==2.1.1
